  "description": "Services on the track network (Phase 4.5 Stage S5, ARCHITECTURE decision 31). Surface Harbour (e1, 2048 to 6144), a curve (e2, 6346), a ramp down 1024 in a tunnel (e3, 32768, 1 in 32; node 3 is a tunnel portal) and underground Deep on a curve (e4, 6346; 1024 to 4096). A train stops with its head at the far end of a platform the way it travels (end going forward, L - start going backward), only at platforms no shorter than it; its path to a station is the least exact distance: the rest of its edge, every edge between and the stretch into the last. A line plans a leg in the least whole second its performance builds a running curve for over that distance, and a service's run takes the time its timetable gives it (Stage W2c, ARCHITECTURE decision 40). Mole (3 cars) repeats Harbour 0/0, Deep 22/30 turning, Harbour 53/62 turning, every 63 minutes: out 2048 + 6346 + 32768 + 4096 = 45258 in 22 minutes, turned at Deep with its head where its tail was (4298 along e4 backward), back 2048 + 32768 + 6346 + 6144 = 47306 in 23 minutes, turned at Harbour (4096 facing east) and pulled up 2048 in a minute to the berth it started from, for the next cycle at 63. Line Tube plans with a crawl at 2 km/h, { acceleration 25, braking 25, topSpeed 2 } (35.6 units a second, reached in 80 s over 1422 units, and as long to stop): its journey from Harbour's berth as one car is 45258 in 1353 s and 49354 in 1469 s, with 2 minutes at each end 3062 s, 52 minutes; it sends Shuttle (1 car, 2048 short of the berth: 47306 out, 1411 s) out every 52. Stage W2b: Mole, started at 0 for a departure at 0, dwells its 42 s at Harbour first and leaves at 0:42; Tube's timetable leaves Harbour 42 s after it sends Shuttle out (also at 0), so both run 42 s behind their timetables, each run shifted by its late departure, until a stop holds them for its departure.",
